        "procedure": "Under purified nitrogen, sodium (0.133 g, 5.78 mmol) and naphthalene (0.76 g, 5.93 mmol) were added to 4 (4.15 g, 2.22 mmol) in THF (140 mL). The mixture was stirred overnight at room temperature, giving a white solid in a red solution. The solid was filtered off, volatiles were evaporated, and the orange residue was washed with pentane (30 mL) and dried in vacuo. Gas-volumetric measurements indicated absorption of 0.65 mol N2 per mole of 4. Crystals were grown from THF at −23 °C. Elemental analysis fits 7·THF (C146H190N2NaO14Sm3); the X-ray formula is the heptakis-THF solvate. The N–N distance is 1.611(16) Å.",
